<% content_for :title, "Integrations — System settings" %>

<%= render "admin/shared/canvas_head", crumbs: [["System settings", admin_settings_path], ["Integrations", nil]] %>

<header class="perma-header">
  <h1 class="perma-header__title">System settings</h1>
</header>

<%# The Integrations tab — a sibling page wearing the same segmented control as
    Domain and Email, because the rotate button is its own form and can't nest
    inside the settings form. %>
<div class="settings u-stack u-stack-double u-margin-block-start settings--wide u-center">
  <% integrations_panel = capture do %>
  <div class="u-stack u-stack-double u-full-width">
    <section class="card" aria-label="BookFunnel">
      <header class="card__header">
        <h2 class="card__title">BookFunnel</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="card__body u-stack">
        <p>BookFunnel can put every reader who claims one of your books straight
           onto this site's list, the moment they sign up. In BookFunnel, go to
           <strong>Integrations → Add Integration</strong>, choose the
           <strong>Sendy</strong> platform, and paste these three values.</p>

        <div class="field">
          <%= label_tag :sendy_host_url, "Sendy Host URL", class: "field__label" %>
          <%= text_field_tag :sendy_host_url, @host_url, class: "field__control", readonly: true %>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <%= label_tag :sendy_api_key, "Sendy API Key", class: "field__label" %>
          <%= text_field_tag :sendy_api_key, @api_key, class: "field__control", readonly: true,
                autocapitalize: "off", autocorrect: "off", spellcheck: "false" %>
          <p class="field__hint u-text-muted">Yours alone — it writes to this site's list and no other.
             Treat it like a password.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <%= label_tag :sendy_list_id, "Sendy Primary List ID", class: "field__label" %>
          <%= text_field_tag :sendy_list_id, @list_id, class: "field__control", readonly: true %>
          <p class="field__hint u-text-muted">BookFunnel also asks for a
             <strong>List Name</strong> — that one is its own label for the list, so anything you'll
             recognize will do.</p>
        </div>

        <%# How a landing page names the promotion that sent the reader —
            Sendy::SubscriptionsController::PROMO_FIELD. %>
        <h3 class="u-microcaps u-text-muted">Naming the promotion</h3>
        <p>To count readers per promo rather than in one lump, tag each BookFunnel landing page.
           On the page, open <strong>Advanced Settings</strong>, tick
           <strong>Send custom fields when adding readers to my mailing list</strong>, and add a
           field named <strong>promo</strong> whose value is the promotion's link code here.</p>
        <p>Then <%= link_to "add the promotion", admin_promotions_path %> with that same code. Readers
           who signed up before you named it are counted too. A page with no <strong>promo</strong>
           field still gets matched by its BookFunnel link, so this is worth doing but not required.</p>

        <p class="u-text-muted">Readers arrive already confirmed: BookFunnel only sends people who
           opted in and consented on its page, so they skip our confirmation email and start your
           welcome sequence right away. Anyone who has unsubscribed here stays unsubscribed.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card" aria-label="Rotate the API key">
      <header class="card__header">
        <h2 class="card__title">Rotate the key</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="card__body u-stack">
        <p>If the key is ever exposed, replace it. The old key stops working immediately, so any
           integration still using it will stop adding readers until you paste in the new one.</p>
        <%= button_to "Generate a new key", admin_integrations_sendy_key_path, method: :patch, class: "button",
              data: { turbo_confirm: "Replace the API key? BookFunnel stops adding readers until you paste the new one in." } %>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <% end %>

  <%= segmented_tabs [
        { id: "identity", label: "Identity", href: admin_settings_path },
        { id: "pages", label: "Pages", href: admin_pages_path },
        { id: "domain", label: "Domain", href: admin_custom_domains_path },
        { id: "email", label: "Email", href: admin_sending_domains_path },
        { id: "integrations", label: "Integrations", panel: integrations_panel },
      ], aria_label: "Settings sections" %>
</div>
